# Database snapshots. An installation writes these beside its database, and a
# test that exercises the snapshot route writes them into the working tree —
# one reached a commit that way. They carry encrypted credentials and API-key
# hashes even when a test's are synthetic, so they are never tracked.
snapshots/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# Scratch probes and mutation harnesses. Two of these were committed once by a
# `git add -A`, and one of them was the codemod that had just rewritten five
# source files — so the rule is that they cannot be staged, not that you should
# remember to delete them.
.tmp-*
